WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.040
Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday. So every year at VidCon, I try to make pretty good choices...until Saturday evening,

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:12.120
when I traditionally celebrate the end of VidCon by participating in a YouTube show called 'Beer and Board Games'.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:16.260
This year, there was a significant emphasis on the, uh, "beer" part of 'Beer and Board Games',

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:20.540
so full disclosure: I'm a little bit hazy on the details of how this all went down.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:26.860
Semi-related story: I lost my video camera so I have no VidCon footage, which is also why we're stuck with the old camera this week.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:34.020
But right, so after 'Beer and Board Games', I ran into 'Minute Physics' Henry and 'Smarter Every Day' Destin and 'CGP Grey'...Grey,

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.840
and somehow, we got to talking about Iceland. Hank, I am a huge fan of Iceland!

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:45.020
It just contains so many things I love: hot baths, an improbably excellent football team, Björk, etc.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:50.580
There's really just the one problem with Iceland, which, y'know, is that it's located...in Iceland.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:57.620
Like, Sarah and I visited Iceland in August of 2008 and we went on this bus tour, and our tour guide, reading from his script, said without any irony:

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:04.720
"Iceland may have 'ice' in its name, but as you can see, the weather is quite mild here year-round. Perhaps we should switch names with Greenland. Ha ha.".

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.520
And then we got that off the bus and that August afternoon it was perhaps half a degree above freezing.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.820
And because of the howling winds, the rain (it was, of course, raining) appeared to be coming up from the ground,

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:20.040
which, for the record, was not green, it was brown, on account of it being recently dried lava.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:27.500
So okay, the four of us discussed problem one - the "Iceland being in Iceland" problem - for a little bit, and then we pivoted to a seemingly unrelated problem,

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:34.000
which is that currently, there is no convenient midway point on the Atlantic side between the Americas and Afro-Eurasia.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.220
Like, on the Pacific side, you have Hawaii or if you're feeling adventurous, the Cook Islands, but on the Atlantic side, pretty much nothing.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:43.160
Until, that is, we relocate Iceland!

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:50.020
Our proposal, Hank, is to move Iceland from *here*, where it is constantly raining and spewing lava to, say, *here*,

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.900
where it would be a lovely stopping point between continents.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:56.400
Quick side note, Hank: I honestly think if we'd had a better-located Iceland in the first place,

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.940
humans probably would have had earlier and more robust trade between the Americas and Afro-Eurasia,

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:07.160
which in turn, might have mitigated some of the horrors of the Colombian Exchange, both on a human and a biodiversity level.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:12.260
So, y'know, not to criticize plate tectonics or anything, but I think this could have been handled better from the beginning!

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:16.520
That said, the world is what it is, or at least it was until we learned to build islands.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:24.780
Right, so we formed a coalition to create 'New Iceland', a nation with: 1. Great weather; 2. Björk; and 3. Apparently a better soccer team than England has.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:28.760
Plus, 4: it's only a two-hour flight from New York, Madrid or Marrakesh.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:33.740
Destin assigned Henry with the job of actually moving Iceland, which, y'know, I'm not a scientist but it can't be that hard.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:36.160
I figure we just get a big tugboat or something and pull it south!

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:42.240
CGP Grey was given the job of designing a flag for New Iceland, Destin assigned himself something having to do with rockets,

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:47.920
and I was tasked with the political problem of getting the people of Iceland to agree to move their country, y'know,

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:51.020
about 3,000 miles South-southwest of its current location.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.900
So here we go: people of Iceland! Hello.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:59.580
You may have noticed that your nation is very cold and rainy in the winter, and then...very cold and rainy in the summer.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:06.020
Also, remember in January when the sun rose at noon, or rather would have risen if it weren't perpetually overcast?

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:13.880
I'd like to solve those problems and give you beaches, warmth, sunshine and joy, all while allowing you to keep your Björk.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:21.080
So whaddaya say, Iceland? I imagine you're gonna say "no"; that you like your country where it is despite its geographical shortcomings.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:28.540
Maybe that says something about Icelanders or maybe it says something about change; that dangerous and beautiful force that drives and defines the universe.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:33.140
Still, I'm hoping you'll say "yes", because I could really use a vacation in sunny New Iceland.

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:36.540
Hank, congratulations on a great VidCon. I'll see you on Friday.

